      "description": "Canadian Pacific Railway Budd Car RDC-3 on the Esquimalt &amp; Nanaimo railway on Vancouver Island, British Columbia. Hulin, photographer. Taken August 1964. View looking east at southern terminus of the E&amp;N line at Pandora Avenue and Store Street in Victoria, BC. The Esquimalt &amp; Nanaimo Railway was incorporated in 1883 by Nanaimo coal baron Robert Dunsmuir and the line was completed in 1886 with the line extended into the City of Victoria in 1888. The Canadian Pacific Railway (CPR) operated the line from 1905 to 1999. Passenger service operated by Canadian National (CN) Via Rail since 1978.",
